      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** (described in [[write-journal]]) is a mechanism that ensures safe file writes in the Grimoire system. Here\u0027s what it does:\n\n**Purpose**: Before any file is overwritten, the guarded write path first records the file\u0027s prior state in an in-memory journal. This serves as a transaction log for write operations.\n\n**What it records**:\n- The previous content of files that existed before the write\n- A record that a file did not exist (for newly created files)\n\n**Rollback on failure**: If an agent run fails \u2014 whether due to a turn cap being exceeded, an unrecoverable error, or denied writes \u2014 the journal can roll back all recorded writes in reverse order:\n- Restore previous content for files that already existed\n- Delete files that were newly created\n\n**Key benefit**: This provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without requiring a database transaction. The journal itself acts as the transaction log and exists only in memory for the duration of a single run.\n\n**Note**: The Query agent (which is what you\u0027re interacting with now) never uses the rollback path since it has no write tool at all \u2014 only agents that actually write to files use this journal\u0027s rollback capability.",
